Z||000000||Master_Sushi||08-30-2001||02:09 PM||||Ok, well I have decided im not going to be keeping my fiero much longer. I'm probably going to sell it next spring. Mostly because I want a bigger car, I'm sick of it, and its to slow for me. Ive spent so many hours working on it over the almost 2 years, only to sell it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. I'll give the stats of it...<BR>1988 Fiero Coupe-<BR>{White paint in pretty good shape, but not perfect}<BR>{4cyl engine running great}<BR>{Automatic}<BR>{AC working perfect}<BR>{Interior in nice shape}<BR>{Sunroof}<BR>{Very clean, no rust (had a little on batt tray, but I removed it)}<BR>{I added a nice pair of 16 inch wheels this summer}<BR>{Luggage rack}<BR>{Pioneer amp and speakers}<BR>{Jensen CD player}<BR>{Everything on the car is in very nice shape and mostly orignal, I've done a few other things here and there I dont remember}<BR>{Rear Defrost}<BR>{Title perfect,only 60k miles}<BR>I really would honestly like to know what I could get for my car. I bought it for $2600 at 45k miles about 2 years ago now. Would I be better off putting it back to stock shape and keeping my add ons? Or selling everything at once. Where should I try and sell it? Is ebay a bad idea?<BR>I really could use some help here.<P>Thanks, please let me know what you think!<BR><P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
